s top technical and leadership but poor crew cooperation and adaptability. Candidate A has decision quality and attention but communication issues and lack of learning. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but crew cooperation issues.\n\nThus candidate B might be the best overall, as his weaknesses are less severe? Pretentiousness and tone could be mitigated. He is conscientious (reliability) and handles stress well (stress resilience). He also has good technical (weather assessment). He lacks explicit leadership but may not be required if crew cooperation is okay. However his communication tone could affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C's leadership is strong, but his unfriendly and not open to new ideas could be a bigger risk for crew cooperation and adaptability. In safety-critical, crew cooperation is vital. So maybe B is better.\n\nThus I will propose Candidate B as provisional recommendation, referencing evidence: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), but note concerns: pretentious, wrong tone (communication, crew cooperation). I will argue that strengths outweigh concerns and that we can address communication with training.\n\nThus my public message: propose Candidate B, reference that no prior discussion yet, give evidence, explain why.\n\nWe need to include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
